Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?refactor(pricing):=20GEO-003=20=E2=80=94=20a=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?band=20knows=20which=20currency=20it=20is?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No public output changes. 34 generated surfaces are byte-identical before and
after: llms.txt, ai.txt, llms-full.txt, every Markdown twin, the organisation
JSON-LD, the three commercial graphs, the six service-page Offer graphs, the
registry price primitives and the entity answers.

PriceBand.currency was the literal type 'CAD' and formatBand wrote a bare $, so
a CAD band and a USD band rendered as the same string — and drift.test.ts
asserts that exact string on every surface. A band in the wrong currency would
have passed tsc, 66 guards, 336 tests and the build, and been read as a price.

The currency is now part of the type and part of the string: a band outside
HOME_CURRENCY names itself. The existing presence assertions therefore tell the
two apart by construction, so no guard was added. Four hand-built price strings
and currency literals outside the constants module were derived instead,
including a regex that recovered minPrice and maxPrice out of formatted prose.

Owner decision D6 (New York priced in USD) is recorded in docs/GEO_SOURCE_MAP.md.

